<title>USA: Unilever stock jumps on earnings, planned unit sale.</title>
<headline>Unilever stock jumps on earnings, planned unit sale.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK</dateline>
<text>
<p>The stock of Unilever NV, the Anglo-Dutch consumer products giant, jumped Friday as Wall Street reacted to the company's recent announcement of sharply higher profits for 1996 and plans to sell its speciality chemicals units.</p>
<p>Unilever was up $8.50 at $188.50 on the New York Stock Exchange in afternoon trading.</p>
<p>The company on Tuesday reported a 15 percent rise in annual profits to $4.4 billion, and said it would sell its speciality chemicals units in a move expected to raise more than $8 billion.</p>
</text>
